{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unodorous-curt-rhea","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nReplace GitHub-only `gh workflow disable/enable` safety around destructive repair with durable,\nprovider-neutral pause ownership. Preserve both `rebar fsck --repair` and `rebar doctor --repair`\nwithout changing their public vocabulary, existing repair effects, or non-repair behavior.\n\nUse the durable `refs/reconciler/gate` control shipped by story `1104`. Add\n`read_pause_with_oid(...) -> tuple[dict[str, object], str] | None` to read one ref OID and decode the\npause document from that same object. Preserve existing `read_pause(...)` callers by delegating to\nthe new seam and discarding only the OID.\n\nThe repair sequence is fail-closed:\n\n1. Resolve `who` through `identity._git_email(repo_root)`. Missing identity aborts before any pause\n   write or repair with `Error: <surface> repair requires a configured git user.email`.\n2. Read the durable gate. Any pre-existing pause is foreign; abort without clearing it.\n3. Generate `repair:<surface>:<uuid4>` once. CAS-write it and record ownership only after success.\n4. Run the existing provider-neutral `refs/reconciler/lock` in-flight check. HELD, corrupt, timeout,\n   transport failure, authentication failure, or uncertainty aborts the repair.\n5. Run the existing repair only after both safety checks succeed.\n6. In `finally`, reread pause document and OID as one snapshot. Clear only if its reason equals this\n   invocation's token. Pass that observed OID to the existing `release(..., oid=observed_oid)` CAS.\n\nA missing, replaced, or changed pause after ownership is an error. Do not recreate it. Do not clear\nanother actor's pause. Do not retry against a fresh OID. A clear failure leaves the bridge paused\nfor explicit operator recovery. This keeps the currently working GitHub safety behavior while also\ncovering local, Jenkins, GitLab, and bare environments without a `gh` binary.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Inventory both repair surfaces and dynamic/string references to existing pause helpers.\n2. Add RED-first backend tests for the one-snapshot pause/OID read and legacy read compatibility.\n3. Add RED-first public command tests for ownership, lock uncertainty, mutation, and cleanup.\n4. Physically hold out edge and end-to-end tests from the implementation worker.\n5. Implement one shared repair-owned pause context used by fsck and doctor.\n6. Remove the GitHub CLI workflow-disable/enable dependency from destructive repair.\n7. Update release notes with the provider-neutral safety contract and operator recovery behavior.\n8. Run focused tests, lint, typecheck, module-size, and full project gates.\n\nThis composes pause acquisition, lock inspection, destructive mutation, and CAS cleanup, so reuse\nthe existing shared concurrency fixtures where applicable. Add a two-clone contention regression\nfor ownership replacement during repair; do not build a bespoke contention harness.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `_ref_lock.read_pause_with_oid` reads the pause ref OID exactly once.\n- [ ] `_ref_lock.read_pause_with_oid` decodes the document from that observed OID.\n- [ ] Existing `_ref_lock.read_pause` behavior remains compatible.\n- [ ] `fsck --repair` uses the durable pause ref before destructive mutation.\n- [ ] `doctor --repair` uses the same repair-owned pause contract.\n- [ ] Neither repair surface requires a `gh` binary.\n- [ ] Missing git email aborts before pause creation.\n- [ ] Missing git email aborts before destructive mutation.\n- [ ] A pre-existing pause aborts repair.\n- [ ] A pre-existing pause is never cleared by repair.\n- [ ] Pause creation uncertainty aborts repair.\n- [ ] A held reconciler lock aborts repair.\n- [ ] A corrupt or indeterminate reconciler lock aborts repair.\n- [ ] Lock transport or authentication uncertainty aborts repair.\n- [ ] Destructive mutation begins only after this invocation owns the pause.\n- [ ] Destructive mutation begins only after the lock check reports safe.\n- [ ] Successful cleanup compares the pause reason to the invocation token.\n- [ ] Successful cleanup deletes by the same observed OID used for the reason check.\n- [ ] A missing pause during cleanup returns nonzero without recreating it.\n- [ ] A replaced or changed pause is never cleared.\n- [ ] A cleanup CAS miss is surfaced without retrying against a new OID.\n- [ ] A cleanup failure leaves the durable pause for operator recovery.\n- [ ] A bare-remote test proves canonical sync is blocked while repair owns the pause.\n- [ ] Local, GHA-shaped, Jenkins-shaped, GitLab-shaped, and bare invocations share pause behavior.\n- [ ] A two-clone test proves ownership replacement cannot clear another actor's pause.\n- [ ] Existing fsck repair postconditions remain unchanged after safe entry.\n- [ ] Existing doctor repair postconditions remain unchanged after safe entry.\n- [ ] Non-repair fsck and doctor behavior remains unchanged.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py`\n- `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py`\n- `src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock_ref_backend.py`\n- `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_stale_channel_repair_heldout.py`\n- focused new fsck/doctor repair ownership tests\n- `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py`\n- `docs/release-notes.md`","id":"591d-baa7-51f1-4696","parent_id":"2db2-3f5e-cf3a-464c","priority":1,"tags":["bridge","portability","repair"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Make destructive repair pause ownership provider-neutral"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786404927614493001,"uuid":"27def21e-e68f-4389-9c27-bc04a02d1710"}